1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:06,750
“Pawn our gold? What will people say!” It's for Dadi's treatment.

2
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:13,209
Papa, a retired banker: “Maa, in 1991 the whole country did this.”

3
00:00:13,359 --> 00:00:18,739
1991. India was running out of dollars.

4
00:00:18,789 --> 00:00:23,761
May: SBI sold ~20 tonnes of gold, to buy back later.

5
00:00:23,811 --> 00:00:29,367
July: the RBI pledged 46.91 tonnes of gold

6
00:00:29,386 --> 00:00:34,962
with the Banks of England and Japan, for $405 million.

7
00:00:35,112 --> 00:00:39,980
Would pawning the gold save India, or sink it?

8
00:00:40,130 --> 00:00:44,833
The gold only bought time. The real fix:

9
00:00:44,854 --> 00:00:49,577
rupee devalued twice; 24 July: reform Budget.

10
00:00:49,627 --> 00:00:53,664
Sept–Nov: loan repaid, gold redeemed.

11
00:00:53,914 --> 00:00:58,025
Pledging isn't failure. No plan is.

12
00:00:58,375 --> 00:01:02,708
Chanakya Niti: āpad-arthe dhanaṃ rakṣet.

13
00:01:02,728 --> 00:01:07,082
Save wealth for hard times (āpad).

14
00:01:07,332 --> 00:01:13,617
Papa: “It was kept for this day. I've set the date to get it back.”

15
00:01:13,767 --> 00:01:19,495
Family gold: use it in a crisis, or never touch it? 1 or 2?
